# Solidity sources must be LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, Windows checkouts with `core.autocrlf=true` materialise CRLF
# while git stores LF. `forge fmt` then reports every line of every file as
# changed, which makes `forge fmt --check` unusable locally and causes it to
# behave differently from Linux CI. Pinning eol=lf keeps the two in agreement.
#
# Scope is deliberately limited to the contract toolchain. Frontend/backend
# files are intentionally left to git's default handling.
*.sol            text eol=lf
*.gas-snapshot   text eol=lf
foundry.toml     text eol=lf
remappings.txt   text eol=lf
